Subject: [PATCH] ui/sdl2, virtio-gpu: zero copy that holds - layout check, held flush fences, verify mode

Zero copy (QEMU_SDL_ZERO_COPY=1) attaches the guest's scanout buffer to the
host compositor's surface as it is.  Made correct on 2026-10-02 (three
corruptions found on a 4K 240 Hz screen, see docs/RESULTS.md):

- The guest buffer goes to the compositor as linear (virtio-gpu carries no
  modifier), so it must be: each new guest buffer's amdgpu tiling is read
  (GEM metadata, on a render-node fd of its own) and anything tiled or
  compressed is copied instead (trace sdl2_swapchain_guest_refused); other
  drivers copy unless QEMU_SDL_ZERO_COPY=force.  The guest makes its
  scanout buffers linear with the virtio-gpu module option linear_scanout=1.
- The flush fence of each zero-copy frame is held until the compositor
  released the buffer shown before it (the display names that buffer with
  a token); up to eight are held at a time and they go out in order - a
  flush that waits for nothing but is behind held ones waits for them -
  because fences of a timeline complete in order on both sides.  Held
  fences were completed early by any later fence: virgl_write_fence() and
  the asynchronous path virtio_gpu_virgl_async_fence_bh() completed every
  command with a lower fence id, a context fence of the guest's rendering
  included.  Both skip fence_deferred commands now; each response is
  traced with its own fence id.  The oldest held fence goes out after 8
  refreshes at most, and the reason is traced (virtio_gpu_flush_fence_out:
  released, in order, timeout, full, now).
- After a release the flush also waits for the compositor's GPU reads of
  the buffer still running (DMA_BUF_IOCTL_EXPORT_SYNC_FILE): the guest's
  writes skip implicit sync.
- Zero-copy presents report the whole buffer as damaged: the compositor may
  not have shown the guest's previous frame.
- QEMU_SDL_ZC_VERIFY=1 (diagnosis): rows of each guest buffer are read when
  it goes to the compositor (twice, 3 ms apart) and when it comes back; a
  difference is traced (sdl2_swapchain_zc_changed / _zc_unsettled).
- sdl2_swapchain_guest_present tells when the guest presented a buffer the
  compositor still held.

Not committed in the fork yet; generated with git diff on top of 0001-0004.

